# hngh-automation configuration
# Every value here is overridable per-invocation by exporting it in the
# environment (config.env is sourced with ${VAR:-default} semantics).
# No secrets live here; tokens stay in ~/.hngh-automation/ (mode 600).

# --- model ---
# Default is the small lane (2026-09-22 VRAM guardrails): Ornith 9B is
# ~6.6 GB weights + at most 1.4 GB KV at ctx-deep = at most 8 GB load,
# at least 12 GB desktop headroom on the 20 GiB RX 7900 XTX. The previous
# default unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF lost the Plasma session on 2026-09-22
# 09:04: it loaded 20.5 GB (9.2 GB GGUF + 0.9 GB mmproj + 8.4 GB KV at
# context 127488) into 20420 MiB free VRAM and Mesa aborted Xorg. Heavy
# lanes re-enable a big model per invocation by exporting
# MODEL=unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF; with the load context pin
# (lib/model.sh unsloth_load_ctx, 2026-09-22 context lane) even a big
# load is bounded (27B: ~10 GB weights + at most 2.3 GB KV at ctx-deep).
# unsloth/Qwen-AgentWorld-35B-A3B-GGUF was tested and REJECTED: it spends
# its whole budget reasoning (finish_reason=length, content=""), so it is
# not the default (kept documented below, deliberately not in the chain).
# Ollama gemma is the final fallback (verified working, slower).
MODEL="${MODEL:-unsloth/Ornith-1.0-9B-GGUF}"
# Local depth is small models only (operator decision 2026-09-22: after
# the local models the fallback tier is the quota legs zai/xiaomi/ocgo/
# kimi in lib/model.sh; the 35B/27B local fallbacks leave the chain
# because their 10-20 GB weight loads are the crash class). gemma-4-12b
# QAT is the second local (servable on :8888, registry row in
# automation/config/unsloth-contexts.tsv).
UNSLOTH_FALLBACK_MODELS="${UNSLOTH_FALLBACK_MODELS:-unsloth/gemma-4-12b-it-qat-GGUF}"
OLLAMA_MODEL="${OLLAMA_MODEL:-hf.co/unsloth/Ornith-1.0-9B-GGUF:latest}"
# 1024 left content empty on the full prompt; 3072 is the verified floor.
MODEL_MAX_TOKENS="${MODEL_MAX_TOKENS:-1024}"
MODEL_TIMEOUT="${MODEL_TIMEOUT:-300}"   # first call after model swap can load 1-3 min

# --- endpoints ---
UNSLOTH_URL="${UNSLOTH_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:8888}"
OLLAMA_URL="${OLLAMA_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:11434}"
TOKEN_FILE="${TOKEN_FILE:-$HOME/.hngh-automation/unsloth.token}"
REFRESH_FILE="${REFRESH_FILE:-$HOME/.hngh-automation/unsloth.refresh}"
REMOTE_URL="${REMOTE_URL:-https://openrouter.ai/api/v1}"
# Cheap-model routing (2026-09-19): defaults/probes ride the contributor-
# priced muse-spark-1.3-contributor leg; fallback is deepseek-v4.1-flash
# (REMOTE_MODEL_FALLBACK); sustained traffic pins zai glm-5.3-flash;
# gemini is burst-only with caps (REMOTE_MODEL_CODING + GEMINI_BURST caps).
REMOTE_MODEL="${REMOTE_MODEL:-meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor}"
REMOTE_MODEL_FALLBACK="${REMOTE_MODEL_FALLBACK:-deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash}"
# Task-class route (operator benchmark priorities, 2026-09-13; burst-only
# 2026-09-19): coding completions that generate whole files/patches pin
# gemini-3.8-flash via MODEL_PIN=remote; cost-tolerated for that class
# only, burst-only with GEMINI_BURST caps below. Not the default
# chain model.
REMOTE_MODEL_CODING="${REMOTE_MODEL_CODING:-google/gemini-3.8-flash}"
# Gemini burst caps live in the cadence-params gemini-burst-max-calls /
# gemini-burst-window-s rows (kimi-daily-cap pattern: no config.env
# pre-set, so the rows stay live; an exported env value still overrides
# the row inside gemini_burst_blocked via ${VAR:-$(get_param ...)}).
# Do NOT pre-set GEMINI_BURST_MAX_CALLS / GEMINI_BURST_WINDOW_S here: a
# pre-set would shadow the rows in every consumer that sources common.sh
# (2026-09-20 burst-params-shadowing gap).
# Task-class route (operator addendum, 2026-09-13): design-feedback/
# coverage second opinions on design docs and plans pin the contributor-
# priced Muse Spark legs via MODEL_PIN=feedback. Second-opinion pass:
# export REMOTE_MODEL_FEEDBACK=meta/muse-spark-1.2-contributor.
REMOTE_MODEL_FEEDBACK="${REMOTE_MODEL_FEEDBACK:-meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor}"
REMOTE_TOKEN_FILE="${REMOTE_TOKEN_FILE:-$HOME/.hngh-automation/openrouter.token}"
REMOTE_DAILY_CAP_CALLS="${REMOTE_DAILY_CAP_CALLS:-200}"
USER_AGENT="${USER_AGENT:-Mozilla/5.0 hngh-automation/0.1}"
# deck model leg (Phase 2, docs/DECK-NODE.md): llama-server on the Steam
# Deck, user service, alias deck-7b. The endpoint now lives in the
# cadence-params deck-model-endpoint row (moved here 2026-09-07); env
# DECK_URL still overrides that row. NOTE: deck_chat appends
# /v1/chat/completions, so the row carries NO /v1 suffix. Port 8082 (8081
# is held by a foreign service on the deck). Deck down -> leg fails closed
# to the next backend; that is normal.
DECK_MODEL="${DECK_MODEL:-deck-7b}"

# --- dashboard ---
DASHBOARD_PORT="${DASHBOARD_PORT:-8890}"   # binds 0.0.0.0 (LAN/phone access)
DASHBOARD_HOST="${DASHBOARD_HOST:-0.0.0.0}"

# --- hngh dogfooding (repo is READ-ONLY for us; we only call its CLI) ---
HNGH_HOME="${HNGH_HOME:-$HOME/Projects/etc/hngh}"
HNGH_CLI="${HNGH_CLI:-$HNGH_HOME/scripts/hngh}"
HNGH_STORE="${HNGH_STORE:-$HOME/.hngh-automation/store}"
HNGH_ROLE="${HNGH_ROLE:-operator}"
# router-tick scrub stems: deployment username as a pathy stem (GAP E
# 2026-09-17: a dash-mangled path whose /home segment was consumed
# upstream must still cut at the username). Comma/space-separated extras;
# an exported env value wins. Exported (the one config.env export):
# unexported vars do not cross cadence-tick's `bash $f` drop-in boundary
# or the python child env, so the stem would never reach router-tick.
export HNGH_ROUTER_PATHY_STEMS="${HNGH_ROUTER_PATHY_STEMS:-bricker}"
# all four limits are required by create-run (nonnegative integers)
HNGH_LOADOUT="loadout-route-label=automation loadout-context-limit=2000 loadout-token-limit=1000 loadout-cost-limit=0 loadout-time-limit=600"

# --- sources (space-separated name:url; __TODAY__ / __WEEKAGO__ are substituted) ---
# 2026-09-07 expansion: RSS/Atom feeds (hnrss, phoronix, arxiv-csai, ghblog)
# are normalized by fetch_rss in lib/sources.sh; cisakev is a JSON feed the
# raw path already handles. Parked by design, see docs/BACKLOG.md: usenet
# via NNTP and social-account notification scrapes (need a design + the
# screening layer, which now exists) — do not add them ad hoc.
SOURCES="${SOURCES:-breaking:https://terminalfeed.io/api/breaking
hn-topstories:https://terminalfeed.io/api/hn-topstories?limit=50
gh-trending:https://terminalfeed.io/api/gh-trending?since=__TODAY__
service-status:https://terminalfeed.io/api/service-status
claude-status:https://terminalfeed.io/api/claude-status
fear-greed:https://terminalfeed.io/api/fear-greed
launches:https://terminalfeed.io/api/launches
hnrss:https://hnrss.org/frontpage
phoronix:https://www.phoronix.com/rss.php
arxiv-csai:https://export.arxiv.org/rss/cs.AI
cisakev:https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/feeds/known_exploited_vulnerabilities.json
ghblog:https://github.blog/feed/
acpkernel-rel:https://github.com/ranxianglei/acp-kernel/releases.atom
bilirel:https://github.com/ranxianglei/billion-context/releases.atom
opencode-acp-rel:https://github.com/ranxianglei/opencode-acp/releases.atom
ework-aio-rel:https://github.com/ranxianglei/ework-aio/releases.atom
jcoderel:https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/releases.atom
}"
MAX_SOURCE_CHARS="${MAX_SOURCE_CHARS:-12000}"   # per source, fed to the model (split across sources)
MAX_PING_WORDS="${MAX_PING_WORDS:-200}"
MAX_MORNING_WORDS="${MAX_MORNING_WORDS:-400}"

# --- schedule (reference; the actual triggers are systemd timers) ---
# model-bench candidates (coding/review-shaped probes, daily 13:10);
# stays the full catalog probe list, small-first (2026-09-22 VRAM guardrails)
BENCH_MODELS="${BENCH_MODELS:-unsloth/Ornith-1.0-9B-GGUF unsloth/gemma-4-12b-it-qat-GGUF unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF unsloth/Ornith-1.0-35B-GGUF unsloth/Qwen-AgentWorld-35B-A3B-GGUF bartowski/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF yuxinlu1/gemma-4-12B-coder-fable5-composer2.5-v1-GGUF}"
# kimi quota leg (verified 2026-09-07, docs/KIMI-QUOTA.md): the K3 quota is
# the kimi.com consumer Kimi Code plan, served by KIMI_AI_KEY on
# api.kimi.com/coding/v1 (lib/model.sh defaults there). k3-256k over the
# 1M-context k3 halves quota burn. Thinking-only models: reasoning tokens
# count against max_tokens. Endpoint/model live in the cadence-params
# kimi-endpoint/kimi-model rows (2026-09-07).
